Susanne","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08039488.2017.1274149","issn":["08039488","08039496"],"issn_org":["08039488"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"163-163","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","title_org":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry. Supplement","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-717842f6-dae3-46be-bccd-6c3e0d25c30a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Treatment of adult patients with schizophrenia and complex mental health needs - A national clinical guideline (vol 70, pg 231, 2016)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-194131","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Tropodithietic acid (TDA)-producing Ruegeria mobilis strains of the Roseobacter clade have primarily been isolated from marine aquaculture and have probiotic potential due to inhibition of fish pathogens. We hypothesized that TDA producers with additional novel features are present in the oceanic environment. We isolated 42 TDA-producing R. mobilis strains during a global marine research cruise. While highly similar on the 16S ribosomal RNA gene level (99–100% identity), the strains separated into four sub-clusters in a multilocus sequence analysis. They were further differentiated to the strain level by average nucleotide identity using pairwise genome comparison. The four sub-clusters could not be associated with a specific environmental niche, however, correlated with the pattern of sub-typing using co-isolated phages, the number of prophages in the genomes and the distribution in ocean provinces. Major genomic differences within the sub-clusters include prophages and toxin-antitoxin systems. In general, the genome of R. mobilis revealed adaptation to a particle-associated life style and querying TARA ocean data confirmed that R. mobilis is more abundant in the particle-associated fraction than in the free-living fraction occurring in 40% and 6% of the samples, respectively. Our data and the TARA data, although lacking sufficient data from the polar regions, demonstrate that R. mobilis is a globally distributed marine bacterial species found primarily in the upper open oceans. It has preserved key phenotypic behaviors such as the production of TDA, but contains diverse sub-clusters, which could provide new capabilities for utilization in aquaculture.The ISME Journal advance online publication, 23 August 2016; doi:10.1038/ismej.2016.111.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Sonnenschein, Eva C.","Nielsen, Kristian Fog","D'Alvise, Paul","Porsby, Cisse Hedegaard","Melchiorsen, Jette","Heilmann, Jens","Kalatzis, Panos G.","López-Pérez, Mario","Bunk, Boyke","Spröer, Cathrin","Middelboe, Mathias","Gram, Lone"],"cuid":["S02-090.88-036393"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Greece","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hellenic Centre for Marine Research","Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research","Miguel Hernández University"],"keyword":["Ecology Evolution Behavior and Systematics","Microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"global occurrence and heterogeneity of the i roseobacter i clade species i ruegeria mobilis i","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5270566?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-090.88-036393","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5270555","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84983417112","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27552638","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-a6efe967-aa96-47dd-8acb-e6b9cbb215f8","ku-defaa8c8-98b4-4f55-996d-b516595d2315"],"keyword":["Ecology, Evolution, Behavior and Systematics","Microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-535DA9C7935C1FF258669FA57AC37C90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5270566?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Bacterial Ecophysiology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Marine Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"hellenic centre for marine research","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hellenic Centre for Marine Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"miguel hernández university","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Miguel Hernández University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"helmholtz centre for infection research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"sonnenscheinpau","last":"Sonnenschein","locid":"3bf1ebdd-b72c-4cfb-b842-bed9397b53ec","name":"Sonnenschein, Eva C.","name_org":"Sonnenschein, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-6959-5100","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Fog","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d2067ee9-e48c-4cf4-ac8f-ee775d8aff5a","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Fog","orcid":"0000-0002-5848-0911","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Paul","key":"dalvisepau","last":"D'Alvise","locid":"54833667-dc7a-400b-be8b-b0eaf3f63ed6","name":"D'Alvise, Paul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cisse Hedegaard","key":"porsbypau","last":"Porsby","locid":"fb5